From: Jetha Chan <jethachan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: don't wait for security indications QCA9379 SDIO does not send

ath10k_install_key() sends WMI_VDEV_INSTALL_KEY_CMDID and then waits up
to 3 s for HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_SEC_IND, failing with -ETIMEDOUT if it does
not come. The QCA9379 SDIO firmware (WLAN.NPL.1.6-00163-QCANPLSWPZ-1)
sends the indication for the pairwise and group keys installed when a
station associates (those never time out), but not when the group key
is replaced and not for any key removal. On a WPA2-PSK network with a
600 s group rekey interval, every rekey ends the connection (Linux
6.19; this code is unchanged since):

  ath10k_sdio mmc1:0001:1: failed to install key for vdev 0 peer xx:xx:xx:xx:1a:61: -110
  wlan0: failed to set key (2, ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff) to hardware (-110)
  wlan0: deauthenticating from xx:xx:xx:xx:1a:61 by local choice (Reason: 1=UNSPECIFIED)

and every roam between two access points of the network spends 6 s on
removing the old keys before authenticating to the new one:

  [222928.982018] ath10k_sdio mmc1:0001:1: failed to install key for vdev 0 peer xx:xx:xx:xx:1c:1c: -110
  [222928.982106] wlan0: failed to remove key (1, ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff) from hardware (-110)
  [222928.991626] wlan0: disconnect from AP xx:xx:xx:xx:1c:1c for new auth to xx:xx:xx:xx:1a:61
  [222932.054043] ath10k_sdio mmc1:0001:1: failed to install key for vdev 0 peer xx:xx:xx:xx:1c:1c: -110
  [222932.054130] wlan0: failed to remove key (0, xx:xx:xx:xx:1c:1c) from hardware (-110)
  [222932.136985] wlan0: authenticate with xx:xx:xx:xx:1a:61 (local address=xx:xx:xx:xx:af:4b)

Treating the timeout as success would keep the connection but still
stall each rekey, and the supplicant's reply to group message 1/2, for
3 s (6 s when mac80211 first removes the key it replaces), well past
the 1 s after which hostapd by default resends group message 1/2 and
close to the point where it gives up. Not waiting is
safe for these operations: a station only receives with its group key,
so no transmit depends on the firmware having programmed it, and the AP
switches to the new group key only after the supplicant has answered,
which it does after set_key() returns. Nothing after a removal depends
on its completion either.

Add a hw_params flag for firmware that behaves like this, set it for
QCA9379 SDIO, and with it skip the wait for station group key
installs (other than static WEP, which is used for transmit) and for
removals. Other hardware keeps waiting for every operation, so a late
indication cannot complete a later install's wait early on firmware
that does send one. Pairwise and AP group key installs still wait.

The indication handler also resets the per-TID last PN that high
latency devices use for their own replay check on frames with an
extended TID, including group addressed ones. Do that when a station
group key is installed without waiting, or frames under the new key,
whose PN starts again from zero, are dropped as replays.

Waiting for the indication has been part of ath10k_install_key() since
the driver was added. Removal timeouts on QCA6174 and WCN3990 are
discussed in the threads below.

Link: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/ath10k/2024-July/015975.html
Link: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/ath10k/2026-February/016781.html
Link: https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/ath10k/2026-September/017285.html
Signed-off-by: Jetha Chan <jethachan@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
index 92fb7f930..f4a126704 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
@@ -697,6 +697,7 @@ static const struct ath10k_hw_params ath10k_hw_params_list[] = {
 		.use_fw_tx_credits = true,
 		.delay_unmap_buffer = false,
 		.mcast_frame_registration = false,
+		.key_update_no_sec_ind = true,
 	},
 	{
 		.id = QCA4019_HW_1_0_DEV_VERSION,
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
index 5b37d0134..308b46391 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
@@ -649,6 +649,13 @@ struct ath10k_hw_params {
 
 	/* The hardware support multicast frame registrations */
 	bool mcast_frame_registration;
+
+	/* The firmware sends an HTT security indication for the keys set up
+	 * when a station associates, but not when a station's group key is
+	 * replaced or when any key is removed. ath10k_install_key() must not
+	 * wait for those.
+	 */
+	bool key_update_no_sec_ind;
 };
 
 struct htt_resp;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
index 8e604697d..1e37a0bc2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -304,6 +304,47 @@ static int ath10k_send_key(struct ath10k_vif *arvif,
 	return ath10k_wmi_vdev_install_key(arvif->ar, &arg);
 }
 
+/* Whether the firmware confirms this key operation with an HTT security
+ * indication (HTT_T2H_MSG_TYPE_SEC_IND).
+ */
+static bool ath10k_mac_key_has_sec_ind(struct ath10k_vif *arvif,
+				       struct ieee80211_key_conf *key,
+				       enum set_key_cmd cmd, u32 flags)
+{
+	if (!arvif->ar->hw_params.key_update_no_sec_ind)
+		return true;
+
+	if (cmd == DISABLE_KEY)
+		return false;
+
+	/* A station only receives with its group key. Static WEP keys are
+	 * the exception: mac80211 sets them as group keys, but they are used
+	 * for transmit as well (see ath10k_set_key()).
+	 */
+	return !(arvif->vdev_type == WMI_VDEV_TYPE_STA &&
+		 (flags & WMI_KEY_GROUP) &&
+		 key->cipher != WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_WEP40 &&
+		 key->cipher != WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_WEP104);
+}
+
+/* Forget the last PN seen per TID, as ath10k_htt_rx_sec_ind_handler() does
+ * for a new key: the new key starts a new PN sequence.
+ */
+static void ath10k_mac_reset_rx_pn(struct ath10k *ar, u32 vdev_id,
+				   const u8 *addr)
+{
+	struct ath10k_peer *peer;
+
+	spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+	peer = ath10k_peer_find(ar, vdev_id, addr);
+	if (peer) {
+		memset(peer->tids_last_pn_valid, 0,
+		       sizeof(peer->tids_last_pn_valid));
+		memset(peer->tids_last_pn, 0, sizeof(peer->tids_last_pn));
+	}
+	spin_unlock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+}
+
 static int ath10k_install_key(struct ath10k_vif *arvif,
 			      struct ieee80211_key_conf *key,
 			      enum set_key_cmd cmd,
@@ -324,6 +365,16 @@ static int ath10k_install_key(struct ath10k_vif *arvif,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	if (!ath10k_mac_key_has_sec_ind(arvif, key, cmd, flags)) {
+		ath10k_dbg(ar, ATH10K_DBG_MAC,
+			   "mac vdev %d %s key %d for %pM without waiting for sec ind\n",
+			   arvif->vdev_id, cmd == SET_KEY ? "set" : "del",
+			   key->keyidx, macaddr);
+		if (cmd == SET_KEY)
+			ath10k_mac_reset_rx_pn(ar, arvif->vdev_id, macaddr);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ar->install_key_done, 3 * HZ);
 	if (time_left == 0)
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
